# Options-trading calculation task set for p1 / p2 / p3 / p7. THIS FILE IS DATA.
#
# Domain: Indian index options (Nifty / Bank Nifty / Sensex) desk arithmetic —
# premium and margin math, spread breakevens and max-loss, expiry-date logic.
# Chosen because every answer is a COMPUTABLE fact: the `expectation` names the
# exact number or date, so the generic rubric's weight-2 success criterion scores
# against ground truth rather than fluency. Every value was computed and checked
# in Python before being written here; lot sizes and premiums are stated inside
# each task so no task depends on outside data.
#
# One JSON object per line: {"id","difficulty","task","expectation"}.
# 5 trivial, 5 moderate, 8 hard = 18 tasks.
{"id": "o01_premium", "difficulty": "trivial", "task": "A Nifty option has a lot size of 75 units. If one lot is bought at a premium of 120 per unit, what is the total premium paid for one lot, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 9000 (rupees)."}
{"id": "o02_atm_strike", "difficulty": "trivial", "task": "Nifty spot is at 23,847. Strike prices are listed at intervals of 50. What is the at-the-money (nearest) strike? Give the strike number only.", "expectation": "States 23850."}
{"id": "o03_moneyness", "difficulty": "trivial", "task": "Nifty spot is 23,847. Is the 24,000 CE (call) option in-the-money or out-of-the-money? Answer with exactly one of: in-the-money, out-of-the-money.", "expectation": "States out-of-the-money (a 24000 call is OTM when spot is 23847)."}
{"id": "o04_pct_move", "difficulty": "trivial", "task": "Nifty opens at 23,600 and closes at 23,836. What is the percentage change, to two decimal places? Give the number with a percent sign.", "expectation": "States 1.00% (23836/23600 - 1 = 1.00%)."}
{"id": "o05_lots_capital", "difficulty": "trivial", "task": "One lot of a Nifty spread requires 15,000 rupees of margin. With 200,000 rupees of capital, what is the maximum whole number of lots that can be taken? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 13 (floor of 200000/15000)."}
{"id": "o06_bull_call_be", "difficulty": "moderate", "task": "A bull call spread on Nifty: buy the 23,800 CE at 150 and sell the 24,000 CE at 70, both per unit. What is the breakeven point at expiry (the Nifty level at which the spread neither gains nor loses)? Give the index level only.", "expectation": "States 23880 (23800 + net debit of 80)."}
{"id": "o07_bull_call_maxloss", "difficulty": "moderate", "task": "A bull call spread on Nifty, lot size 75: buy the 23,800 CE at 150 and sell the 24,000 CE at 70, both per unit. What is the maximum loss for one lot, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 6000 (net debit 80 per unit x 75)."}
{"id": "o08_expiry_weekly", "difficulty": "moderate", "task": "Nifty weekly options expire on Thursday. For the trading week that contains Tuesday 10 March 2026, on what calendar date does the weekly option expire, and what weekday is it? Assume no holiday shift.", "expectation": "States 12 March 2026 and identifies it as a Thursday."}
{"id": "o09_pnl_expiry", "difficulty": "moderate", "task": "One lot of the Nifty 23,800 CE (lot size 75) was bought at a premium of 150 per unit. Nifty expires at 24,050. What is the net profit or loss on the position at expiry, in rupees? Give a signed number.", "expectation": "States +7500 (intrinsic 250 minus premium 150 = 100 per unit x 75)."}
{"id": "o10_brokerage", "difficulty": "moderate", "task": "A four-legged options strategy is opened and later closed. Brokerage is a flat 20 rupees per order, and each leg is one order on entry and one on exit. What is the total brokerage for the round trip, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 160 (4 legs x 2 sides x 20)."}
{"id": "o11_condor_maxprofit", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "An iron condor on Nifty (lot size 75), all per unit: sell the 23,800 PE at 60 and buy the 23,600 PE at 30; sell the 24,000 CE at 55 and buy the 24,200 CE at 25. What is the maximum profit for one lot, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 4500 (net credit 60 per unit x 75)."}
{"id": "o12_condor_maxloss", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "For the same iron condor (sell 23,800 PE at 60, buy 23,600 PE at 30, sell 24,000 CE at 55, buy 24,200 CE at 25; lot size 75), what is the maximum loss for one lot, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 10500 (wing width 200 minus net credit 60 = 140 per unit x 75)."}
{"id": "o13_condor_be", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "For the same iron condor (short strikes 23,800 PE and 24,000 CE, net credit 60 per unit), what are the two breakeven index levels at expiry? Give both numbers.", "expectation": "States a lower breakeven of 23740 and an upper breakeven of 24060."}
{"id": "o14_ratio_profit", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "A call ratio spread on Nifty (lot size 75), all per unit: buy one 23,800 CE at 150 and sell two 24,000 CE at 70 each. What is the profit for one lot if Nifty expires exactly at 24,000, in rupees? Give the number only.", "expectation": "States 14250. Net debit is 150 - 140 = 10 per unit; at 24000 the long call is worth 200, so profit is (200 - 10) = 190 per unit x 75 = 14250."}
{"id": "o15_ratio_ube", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "For the same call ratio spread (buy one 23,800 CE at 150, sell two 24,000 CE at 70 each), what is the upper breakeven index level at expiry — the level above which the position begins to lose money? Give the index level only.", "expectation": "States 24190 (24000 + the 190-per-unit peak profit)."}
{"id": "o16_return_on_margin", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "An iron condor collects a net credit of 60 per unit on a Nifty lot of 75, and ties up 10,500 rupees of margin for one lot after the credit is applied. If the position is held to expiry and keeps the full credit, what is the return on margin as a percentage, to two decimal places? Give the number with a percent sign.", "expectation": "States 42.86% (4500 profit / 10500 margin)."}
{"id": "o17_expiry_holiday", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "Nifty monthly options expire on the last Thursday of the month. For March 2026, that Thursday falls on a trading holiday. On what calendar date and weekday does the monthly expiry then take place, given that a holiday shifts expiry to the previous trading day? (March 2026: the last Thursday is the 26th.)", "expectation": "States 25 March 2026 and identifies it as a Wednesday."}
{"id": "o18_straddle_be", "difficulty": "hard", "task": "A short straddle on Sensex (lot size 20): sell the 80,000 CE at 600 and the 80,000 PE at 550, both per unit. What are the two breakeven index levels at expiry? Give both numbers.", "expectation": "States a lower breakeven of 78850 and an upper breakeven of 81150 (80000 minus/plus the total credit of 1150)."}
